# CSS and design system

## File organization

- Import order in main CSS entry: Tailwind → theme tokens → domain/feature stylesheets → global a11y.
- One concern per file: `hero-theme-tokens.css`, `hero-action-buttons.css`, `blackfang-theme.css`, `site-a11y.css`, etc.
- Avoid giant monolithic CSS; co-locate feature chrome with feature names.

## Tokens

- Define colors/spacing/type on **theme root classes** (e.g. `.hero-era--modern`, `.blackfang-campaign`).
- Use semantic names: `--bf-accent`, `--hero-fg-muted`, `--cs-btn-bg` — not raw hex in components.
- Document WCAG intent in file headers when contrast pairs matter.
- Per-theme overrides via modifier classes (`--dark`, `--light`, `--retro16`).

## Layout patterns

- **Portfolio/marketing**: aurora backdrops, glass panels (`backdrop-filter`), Fraunces + Inter, violet/rose accent palette.
- **Terminal/product UI**: mono labels, uppercase tracking, phosphor accent system, inset borders, dense tables.
- Tables: top-aligned cells (`align-top`), shared table chrome classes (`operative-card-table`, `bf-dataslate-row`).

## Tailwind + CSS split

- Tailwind: flex/grid, spacing, responsive breakpoints, `min-w-0` overflow fixes.
- CSS classes: repeated visual language, animations, pseudo-elements, complex shadows, theme tokens.
- Do not fight Tailwind with `!important`; add a semantic class instead.

## Responsive and safe areas

- Use `clamp()` for fluid type where the portfolio does.
- Account for `env(safe-area-inset-top)` on fixed/sticky chrome and skip links.
- Mobile-first nav: drawer + backdrop; desktop sidebar — skip link must bypass nav tab stops.
